arguments.prompt:
Fix AOT warnings in two files in `/tmp/sv-6633ee2a04db4717b6f60e74d0a0cc90/before/`:

1. **ArmEnvironment.cs** line 80: `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` produces IL2026/IL3050.

Fix: Replace `JsonSerializer.Serialize(this)` with a manual string construction that doesn't use JsonSerializer. The struct only has `Endpoint` (Uri) and `Audience` (string) properties. Use:
```csharp
public override string ToString() => $"{{\"Endpoint\":\"{Endpoint}\",\"Audience\":\"{Audience}\"}}";
```

Wait, that's not great for escaping. Better: Use `JsonSerializer.Serialize` with a source-generated context. Create a `JsonSerializerContext` for this.

Actually the simplest AOT-safe approach: use Utf8JsonWriter to a MemoryStream/ArrayBufferWriter:
```csharp
public override string ToString()
{
    var buffer = new System.Buffers.ArrayBufferWriter<byte>();
    using (var writer = new Utf8JsonWriter(buffer))
    {
        writer.WriteStartObject();
        writer.WriteString("Endpoint", Endpoint.ToString());
        writer.WriteString("Audience", Audience);
        writer.WriteEndObject();
    }
    return System.Text.Encoding.UTF8.GetString(buffer.WrittenSpan);
}
```

Add `using System.Buffers;` and `using System.Text;` at the top if needed.

2. **ArmClientOptions.cs** line 52: `JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span)` produces IL2026/IL3050.

Fix: Replace `JsonSerializer.Deserialize` with `JsonDocument.Parse` and manually navigate the JSON structure. The code at lines 46-78 already iterates through the JSON structure after deserializing, so we can parse with JsonDocument directly.

Current code (lines 46-78):
```csharp
public void SetApiVersionsFromProfile(AzureStackProfile profile)
{
    var assembly = Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly();
    using (Stream stream = assembly.GetManifestResourceStream(profile.GetManifestName()))
    {
        var span = BinaryData.FromStream(stream).ToMemory().Span;
        var allProfile = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<Dictionary<string, Dictionary<string, JsonElement>>>(span);
        var armProfile = allProfile["resource-manager"];
        foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile)
        {
            var namespaceName = keyValuePair.Key;
            var element = keyValuePair.Value;

            foreach (var apiVersionProperty in element.EnumerateObject())
            {
                var apiVersion = apiVersionProperty.Name;
                foreach (var resourceTypeItem in apiVersionProperty.Value.EnumerateArray())
                {
                    string resourceTypeName = default;
                    foreach (var property in resourceTypeItem.EnumerateObject())
                    {
                        if (property.NameEquals("resourceType"))
                        {
                            resourceTypeName = property.Value.GetString();
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                    var resourceType = $"{namespaceName}/{resourceTypeName}";
                    ResourceApiVersionOverrides[resourceType] = apiVersion;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Replace with:
```csharp
public void SetApiVersionsFromProfile(AzureStackProfile profile)
{
    var assembly = Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly();
    using (Stream stream = assembly.GetManifestResourceStream(profile.GetManifestName()))
    {
        using JsonDocument doc = JsonDocument.Parse(BinaryData.FromStream(stream));
        var armProfile = doc.RootElement.GetProperty("resource-manager");
        foreach (var keyValuePair in armProfile.EnumerateObject())
        {
            var namespaceName = keyValuePair.Name;
            var element = keyValuePair.Value;

            foreach (var apiVersionProperty in element.EnumerateObject())
            {
                var apiVersion = apiVersionProperty.Name;
                foreach (var resourceTypeItem in apiVersionProperty.Value.EnumerateArray())
                {
                    string resourceTypeName = default;
                    foreach (var property in resourceTypeItem.EnumerateObject())
                    {
                        if (property.NameEquals("resourceType"))
                        {
                            resourceTypeName = property.Value.GetString();
                            break;
                        }
                    }
                    var resourceType = $"{namespaceName}/{resourceTypeName}";
                    ResourceApiVersionOverrides[resourceType] = apiVersion;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This eliminates the need for `JsonSerializer.Deserialize` entirely. Remove `using System.Text.Json;` only if no other references to it remain (keep it if other code in the file uses it - actually just keep it since `JsonDocument` and `JsonElement` are in that namespace).

3. **Extensions/ArmClientBuilderExtensions.cs** line 30: `builder.RegisterClientFactory<ArmClient, ArmClientOptions>(configuration)` calls a method marked `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]`.

Fix: Add `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]` and `[RequiresDynamicCode]` attributes to the `AddArmClient<TBuilder, TConfiguration>` method since it calls into the config-binding infrastructure that is fundamentally reflection-based.

```csharp
[RequiresUnreferencedCode("Binding strongly typed objects to configuration values is not supported with trimming. Use the Configuration Binder Source Generator instead.")]
